@title INC-3017 postmortem: listing photo uploads
@subtitle Stonebridge Realty, outage on 2026-08-27
@author Listings Platform team
@date 2026-08-27

kpi Duration | 112 min
kpi Peak upload failures | 100%
kpi Listings missing photos | 8,340
kpi Support tickets | 412

## Summary

A storage policy change was meant to restrict bucket access to our VPC endpoint. It also blocked uploads made with pre-signed URLs from agents' phones, so every mobile upload returned 403 until the deny statement was removed.

## Timeline

All times UTC on 2026-08-27.

table = time,event; **10:15**,**Policy change applied through Terraform**; **10:22**,**Uploads begin failing with 403**; 10:31,First customer ticket reaches support; 10:48,Incident declared Sev2; **11:20**,**Policy diff identified as the cause**; 11:58,Hotfix applied removing the deny statement; **12:07**,**Uploads recover**

## Why it was not caught

- The change was tested only from the office network.
- Staging has no mobile upload test.
- The policy linter does not model pre-signed URLs.

## What went well

- The declared incident had a clear commander within 17 minutes.
- Once the cause was known, the rollback itself took under 10 minutes.

## Action items

table = action,owner,due; Alert when upload 403s exceed 2% for 5 minutes,Listings on-call,2026-09-11; Add a pre-signed URL upload test to staging,Greta Lindqvist,2026-09-18; Require policy changes to be applied to staging first,Omar Haddad,2026-09-25
